course: dictionary
lesson: 7424
title: Polite words and actions
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Polite means behaving in a kind and respectful way. A polite person says please and thank you, waits their turn, and does not interrupt. «Chloe stays polite but stops sharing secrets.» Even though Chloe is no longer close to her friend, she still behaves kindly and respectfully.
explain: Polite can also describe what you say or do. «She made a polite request» means she asked nicely, not in a demanding way. Look at the words around polite for clues: please, thank you, sorry and politely ask all point to good manners.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If "kind and respectful" still makes sense, you are right. If it does not, read the sentence again and look for more clues.
fact: Polite means behaving in a kind and respectful way.
fact: The noun is politeness, and the adverb is politely: she asked politely.
fact: Being polite does not mean doing what a stranger tells you. You can say no politely and still stay safe.
fact: «Respect means being curious and kind: asking polite questions.»
fact: In some cultures it is polite to ask which name someone wants to use. In «Wang Lei», Wang is the surname, which comes first.
exercise: «Please wait your turn and don't interrupt.» Which behaviour is polite? | Shouting over the top of others | *Waiting for your turn | Pushing to the front | Ignoring the person who is talking
exercise: «Chloe stays polite but stops sharing secrets.» What does polite show about Chloe? | *She still behaves kindly and respectfully | She is pretending to be asleep | She is being loud and rude | She is telling everyone her secrets
exercise: «She made a polite request.» What does polite request suggest? | She forgot to ask at all | *She asked nicely | She demanded it loudly | She ordered it from a shop
test: Which word is the noun for polite? | Politer | Impolitely | Politely | *Politeness
test: Someone you don't know asks you to go somewhere with them. Which reply is polite and safe? | Fine, I'll come with you | Go away, you weirdo | *No thank you, I'm not going with you | Say nothing and run off
exam: Which word completes the sentence? «It's ___ to wait your turn.» | Late | *polite | Rude | Noisy
